data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":461,"item_id":"fc_0221c7b4a997c46a016adb482882a481919823e563eb41fd82","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy NL0 graph revision; no revised artifact has yet been checked or submitted\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Completed review of the frozen problem, prior candidate, independent Audit A findings, the relevant NL0/Yui rules, and the recovered Frechet integration-by-parts theorem. Queried the theorem successfully as M010 in this stage and inspected the official pinned source: it explicitly describes the finite-dimensional Haar-measure theorem and its integrability and tsupport-derivative conditions. Also queried and inspected IsCompact.measure_lt_top, establishing an available pinned source for compact-set finite measure. The candidate still requires substantial ordinary graph drafting: rewrite R004 around this theorem while proving all three integrability obligations and both derivative conditions from N001; make N001 export time-window quantified support/regularity facts; repair R001's integral-zero justification; register the Euclidean/Borel/Lebesgue ambient facts and compact measure source; fix R003's empty-C bound; and update/remove unused sources plus actual R004 direct declarations. No unsupported mathematical implication is being reported as a gap.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Actual frozen task documents and Audit A findings; source probe and official source read performed in this stage. The returned probe identifies the new theorem as M010 for this stage. The task requires a complete graph followed by structural check and fresh Audit A, neither of which has occurred.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":[\\\"Read SKILL.md, NL0 stage/format/self-containment/authoring/Audit A rules.\\\",\\\"Read all six frozen task inputs, including prior graph, full findings, recovered source signature and target/context.\\\",\\\"Probed integral_bilinear_hasFDerivAt_right_eq_neg_left_of_integrable; its complete signature requires integrability of B(f'·v,g), B(f,g'·v), and B(f,g), and HasFDerivAt on tsupport(g), tsupport(f).\\\", \\\"Inspected official Mathlib source Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/LineDeriv/IntegrationByParts.lean lines 1-80.\\\",\\\"Probed IsCompact.measure_lt_top and inspected its official source lines 331-343.\\\"]}\"}"}

